  "worked_solution": "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,2]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ is closed, but it is not a bounded interval in the form $[a,b].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
